# =============================================================================
# check_domains.denylist — dead / placeholder hosts that must NEVER appear in
# backend source or IaC.
#
# Consumed by backend/scripts/check_domains.sh (denylist check): every host
# listed below is grepped across backend/app, Caddyfile, and render.yaml, and
# ANY occurrence fails the build. This catches the regression class where a
# dead host or placeholder URL gets baked into a CORS origin, a response
# sample, an email template, or an IaC env value.
#
# Format: one host per line. Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored. Hosts
# are matched as literal substrings (no regex) — add the host exactly as it
# should never appear (e.g. "storage.example.com", not just "example.com").
#
# ── NOT in this list (deliberately — read before adding) ──────────────────────
#   torrent-cdn.onrender.com   LIVE Render backend origin (health 200). The
#     Vercel proxy (frontend/vercel.json) rewrites to it and the p2p-e2e CI
#     uses it as the production backend — it is NOT dead. Do not add.
#   torrentcdn.com / www.torrentcdn.com / api.torrentcdn.com — dead DNS, but
#     referenced in backend comments/tests DOCUMENTING their removal (the
#     guard's docstring explains why those pass). A denylist entry here would
#     false-positive the removal notes. The app's own dead-DNS auto-correction
#     in config.py handles the runtime case.
#   project-ref.supabase.co / postgres.xxxxx / aws-0-xxx.pooler.supabase.com —
#     documented CONFIG placeholders (config.py comments + render.yaml), not
#     shipped references. Denylisting them would flag the docs that tell the
#     deployer what to set. The guard is for shipped source/IaC references.
# =============================================================================

# Placeholder storage hosts — never real, must never ship in a CORS origin,
# presigned URL, or response sample.
storage.example.com
storage.example
proj.supabase.co
placeholder.example
minio.example
bucket.example.com

# Generic example hosts — a dead giveaway that a real value was left as a
# template placeholder.
example.org
www.example.org

# Dead API hosts from the docs-accuracy audit (6dadd9d) — the api.* variants
# of owned domains. NOTE: api.torrentcdn.store is ALSO hard-checked separately
# in the script (with a documented-warning exemption); listed here too so a
# future reader sees the full dead-host set in one place.
api.torrentcdn.store
